# Cursor Rules — Human UI Engineering

This project adheres to the **Human UI Engineering** framework.

The single source of truth for all architectural, design, engineering, and quality workflows is [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).

## Operational Instructions for Cursor

1. **Strict 14-Step Workflow**: Always follow the sequence defined in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md#2-mandatory-14-step-engineering-workflow).
2. **Context Discovery**: Discover project dependencies, styling solutions, and architecture before introducing new files or code.
3. **No AI Cliché Styling**: Do not produce dark-mode neon glows, random card grids, or unnecessary glassmorphism unless explicitly specified in brand design tokens. See [Human Design Rules](../../design/human-design-rules.md).
4. **Shared Foundations First**: Build or update shared primitives in `components/` before writing screen-level UI.
5. **Quality Verification**: Verify type safety, accessibility, layout stability, and responsiveness. Consult [Quality Review](../../quality/ui-review.md).

